      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If a breach occurs, you are legally required to notify the French data protection authority (CNIL) without undue delay, typically within 72 hours, unless the risk to data subjects is low. You must also inform any affected customers directly if their data has been compromised. Failure to report or document the incident effectively can result in severe fines alongside potential penalties for negligence.\n\nIt is also crucial to establish a clear contingency plan that lists specific steps to take immediately upon discovery of security breaches. For further guidance, you can consult the CNIL guidelines specifically designed for small enterprises in France.",
